  "dropped_note": "Dropped 57 ways within 400 m that are not this structure. 30 are railway ways (Edson Subdivision, CN and CP lines, Bonaventure Lead and others), which are not over Yellowhead Trail at this point. The nearest Alberta rail records are STRU 40108 (B096, CNR, 56.6 m, over local roads, about 0.33 km north-north-west) and STRU 39842 (CPR over 127 Street, about 1.0 km east). The other 27 are local streets, footways, service roads, and cycleways not on the St. Albert Trail or Yellowhead alignment (for example 124 Avenue NW, 133 Street NW, 134 Street NW, St Albert Trail NW residential way 31689229). Ways kept as approaches are primary, secondary, trunk, and link roads within 110 m of the centre. Some Yellowhead ways in OSM carry ref=2 (the Highway 2 ref) although Alberta and the other tags give Highway 16; the ref is left as mapped.",
  "height_note": "No heights are invented here. Alberta gives a theoretical vertical clearance under the structure of 5.4 m and no deck elevation. OSM maxheight=5.3 on the Yellowhead motorway ways is a mapper tag, not a published clearance. Both are recorded in NOTES.md. No deck elevation is published."
